<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Grenada</h1><p class="st-meta">1974 CE – present · capital St George's</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Spice island independent since 1974, scene of a socialist revolution in 1979 and a US invasion in 1983.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-grenada">Colony of Grenada</a> became independent on 7 February 1974 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-gairy">Eric Gairy</a>, amid strikes and protests against his rule and his feared <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongoose-gang">Mongoose Gang</a>. It remained a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-nations">Commonwealth</a> realm with the British monarch as head of state.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>On 13 March 1979 the New Jewel Movement led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-bishop">Maurice Bishop</a> overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-gairy">Gairy</a> and formed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-revolutionary-government-grenada">People's Revolutionary Government</a>, the first revolution in the English-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. It expanded literacy, health and cooperatives, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a>, which helped build the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurice-bishop-international-airport">Point Salines</a> airport, and postponed elections. A rival faction under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-coard">Bernard Coard</a> placed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> under arrest, and on 19 October 1983 Bishop and several ministers were executed.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>On 25 October 1983 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> allies invaded, removing the military council. Elections in 1984 restored parliamentary rule. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keith-mitchell">Keith Mitchell</a> served as prime minister for many years, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-ivan">Hurricane Ivan</a> wrecked the island in 2004, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dickon-mitchell">Dickon Mitchell</a> took office in 2022.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/grenada.jpg" alt="Grenada" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: See file history below for details. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Grenada.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1974 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>St George's</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Eric Gairy, Maurice Bishop, Keith Mitchell</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism and Anglicanism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English and Grenadian Creole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/grenada">Grenada</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2000&amp;focus=grenada" aria-label="Grenada on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2984 1727 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Grenada lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3304 1983L3303 1984"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3303 1984h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3304 1983h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3304 1983h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=2000&amp;focus=grenada">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
